---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **같은 작품이 네 위키피디아에 도착하는 차례.** (`/written-down-first`)
 *
 * ── 접었다가 되살린 지면 ──────────────────────────────────────
 *   이 각도를 한 번 접었다. 한국어판을 기준으로 「몇 달 뒤에 적혔나」를 재려다,
 *   「오징어 게임」 ko 문서의 첫 판이 **2025-01** 로 나오는 것을 보고 멈췄다. 2021년 작품인데.
 *   ⭐ 그런데 오염을 **잴 수 있었다** — 첫 판보다 **앞선 달에 읽혔는지**를 보면 된다.
 *     동남아 네 판 153개 문서 중 지워진 것은 **0개**였다. 한국어판만 검증조차 못 했다.
 *   ⭐ 그래서 한국어판을 빼고 **네 판끼리** 재니 물음이 그대로 섰다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 ────────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **순위표로 줄세우지 않는다.** 넷에 등수를 매기지 않고 「몇 편에서 먼저였나」만 센다.
 * ⛔ **「왜」를 말하지 않는다.** 크기가 아니라는 것까지만 말한다 —
 *    베트남어판이 문서·편집자·판 수 셋 다 앞서는데도 먼저 적는 것은 인도네시아어판이다.
 * ⛔ **적힌 때를 읽힌 때로 읽지 않는다.** 독자는 문서보다 먼저 올 수도, 안 올 수도 있다.
 * ⛔ **없는 문서를 늦은 것으로 세지 않는다.** 한 판에 없으면 그 작품을 통째로 뺀다.
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않는다. Riot Production(App 866800) 승인 전이다.
 *
 * 🔴 Astro 앞말(`---` 사이)은 **TypeScript 다.** JSX 를 넣으면 빌드가 죽는다.
 * 🔴 앞말에서 `export function` 을 쓰지 않는다 — Astro 가 딴 스코프로 옮긴다.
 * 🔴 JSX 는 끝 공백을 버린다. 붙여 써야 할 곳은 `{' '}` 를 넣는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import d from '../../data/wikitip-written-down-first.json';

const 셈 = d.arrivedFirst;
const 크 = d.sizeControl;
/* 먼저 적은 편수가 많은 차례로 — ⛔ 등수가 아니라 자료가 정한 차례다 */
const 판차례 = [...d.editions].sort((a, b) => 셈.counts[b] - 셈.counts[a]);
/* 벌어진 폭이 큰 것부터 — 표가 무엇을 보이려는지가 분명해진다 */
const 표줄 = [...d.titles].sort((a, b) => b.spreadMonths - a.spreadMonths);

const TITLE = 'The same Korean title reaches four Wikipedias in a fixed order, '
  + 'and the biggest one is not first';
const DESC =
  `Across ${d.measured} Korean titles with an article on all four Southeast Asian Wikipedias, `
  + `the ${d.editionNames[크.writesFirstMost]} edition was first or joint-first `
  + `${셈.counts[크.writesFirstMost]} times. The last edition arrives a median of `
  + `${d.spreadMedianMonths} months after the first.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.wikidata.org/', 'https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/written-down-first">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>
  <p class="lead">{d.question}</p>
  <p class="q">
    Of the {d.totalTitles} Korean titles we hold, {d.measured} have an article on all four
    editions. The {d.editionNames[크.writesFirstMost]} Wikipedia wrote first, or joint-first,
    for {셈.counts[크.writesFirstMost]} of them. The
    {' '}{d.editionNames[크.largestBy.articles]} Wikipedia — the largest of the four on every
    measure we checked — did so for {셈.counts[크.largestBy.articles]}.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Who writes first</h2>
    <p class="note">
      A title counts for an edition if that edition's article is the oldest, or ties for oldest.
      {' '}{셈.tied} of the {셈.outOf} titles are ties, which is why the numbers below add up to
      more than {셈.outOf}.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Wikipedia</th><th>First or joint-first</th><th>Articles</th>
            <th>Active editors</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {판차례.map((p) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{d.editionNames[p]}</td>
              <td><b>{셈.counts[p]}</b> of {셈.outOf}</td>
              <td class="fine">{크.sizes[p].articles.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
              <td class="fine">{크.sizes[p].activeEditors.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {!크.explainedBySize && (
      <p>
        <strong>The obvious explanation does not hold.</strong> A bigger encyclopaedia with more
        editors would be expected to cover anything sooner, but the
        {' '}{d.editionNames[크.largestBy.articles]} Wikipedia leads on articles, on active
        editors and on total edits, and it is not the one that writes about Korean titles first.
        We can rule that explanation out. We did not measure what replaces it, and we are not
        going to guess.
      </p>
    )}
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How long the rest take</h2>
    <p>
      Counting from the first edition to write a title to the last, the median gap is
      {' '}<b>{d.spreadMedianMonths} months</b>, and it runs from {d.spreadRange[0]} to
      {' '}{d.spreadRange[1]} months.
    </p>
    {d.stability && d.stability.verdict.steady && (
      <p class="note">
        ⭐ This median holds. Remove any single title from the {d.measured} and it stays at
        {' '}{d.stability.median} months — a swing of {d.stability.swingOverMedian}. We check every
        median we publish this way now, after one of ours moved by most of its own size and had to
        be corrected twice in a day; the <a href="/one-out">method is here</a>.
      </p>
    )}
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Title</th><th>First</th>{d.editions.map(() => <th>then</th>)}<th>Spread</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {표줄.map((t) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{t.title}</td>
              <td class="fine">{t.order[0].firstWritten}</td>
              {t.order.map((o) => (
                <td class="fine">
                  {d.countryNames[o.edition]}
                  {o.monthsAfterFirst > 0 ? ` +${o.monthsAfterFirst}` : ''}
                </td>
              ))}
              <td>{t.spreadMonths} {t.spreadMonths === 1 ? 'month' : 'months'}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      Read a row across, not down. The order of the country names is the order those editions
      wrote the title, and <code>+n</code> is months after the first of them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>We checked our own dates before using them</h2>
    <p>
      A first-revision date says when an article has existed <em>under its current name</em>, not
      when the title was first written about. Move or merge an article and the earlier revisions
      go with it, leaving a date that is far too recent.
    </p>
    <p>
      So we tested every date against the months that article was actually read. If a page was
      read before its own first revision, the date has been erased. Of
      {' '}<b>{d.moveCheck.checked}</b> dates we could test this way, <b>{d.moveCheck.moved}</b>
      {' '}failed. {d.moveCheck.unknown} could not be tested, because those articles have no
      month with any reading at all.
    </p>
    <p class="warn">
      ⚠ <strong>The Korean Wikipedia is not on this page, and that is why.</strong> Its article
      for Squid Game reports a first revision of 2025-01 for a title from 2021, and we hold no
      Korean pageview data to check the rest of its dates against. An edition we cannot test is
      not an edition we will publish.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why {d.measured} titles and not {d.totalTitles}</h2>
    <p>{d.whyFewer}</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What this page cannot tell you</h2>
    {d.cannotSay.map((s) => <p class="note">{s}</p>)}
    <p class="note">
      First revisions — Wikipedia API. Reads — Wikimedia Pageviews API, human traffic only,
      monthly. Edition sizes — Wikimedia <code>siteinfo</code>, read {d.sizeControl.measuredOn}.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/written-down-first" />
</WikiTip>

<style>
  .warn { border-left: 3px solid #b45309; padding-left: 1rem; }
</style>
